      "content": "I realize your situation is very uncomfortable and urgent. Pseudoephedrine in Sudafed is a sympathomimetic agent which can constrict blood vessels to relieve nasal congestion, as well as raise blood pressure. The 60mg dose you've mentioned is significant and could potentially interact with lisinopril by further elevating your blood pressure. While \"just one pill\" might not immediately send you to the hospital, there is health risk associated with altering your medication regimen without professional guidance. My advice for your well-being would still be to avoid Sudafed and seek immediate help from a different source. The potential for serious complications transcends just a textbook warning, especially with your existing hypertension.",
